\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ src/full_node.fam — the node.  One thread, one loop over its devices: the
\ kernel first (src/proc.fam kinit: the trap vector, the timer and the PLIC
\ doorbells that `wait` needs), then every turn takes the frames in, serves
\ HTTP and WebSocket (src/http.fam) on port 8080, runs TCP's timers, and
\ sleeps until a doorbell or 100 ms.
\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

kinit
evinit
evnet? @ if
	0A00020F lit FFFFFF00 lit 0A000202 lit ethinit drop
	udpinit  20 lit tcpinit  1F90 lit 20 lit httpinit
	\ a 'q' waiting on the UART after the boot config (scripts/boot.sh QUIET=1) turns the trace off
	10000005 lit c@ 1 lit and if getc 'q' lit = if 0 lit else -1 lit then else -1 lit then dup tlog ! hlog !
	hlog @ if "q: serving http on port 8080; every connection, request, frame and TCP event is logged below, [uptime in ms]\n" puts
	else "q: serving http on port 8080, trace off\n" puts then
	begin
		evarm
		netpoll
		httpturn
		tcptick
		0 lit F4240 lit evwait drop
	0 lit until
else "q: no NIC, nothing to do\n" puts then
bye
